solution.text:
We know that
$$
R=\frac{V^{2}}{P}
$$
Given $\quad V=200 \mathrm{V}, P=40 \mathrm{W}$
and $\quad V=100 \mathrm{V}$
Hence, $\quad R=\frac{V^{2}}{P}=\frac{200 \times 200}{50}$
$$
\begin{array}{l}
P=\frac{V^{2}}{R}=\frac{100 \times 100 \times 50}{200 \times 200} \\
P^{\prime}=12.5 \mathrm{W}
\end{array}
$$
